\paragraph{Why not standard overestimation countermeasures?}
Double Q-learning \citep{vanhasselt2016double}, TD3 \citep{fujimoto2018td3}, and ensemble critics \citep{chen2021redq} target maximization bias in the \emph{policy improvement} step. CIVO originates earlier: the RSSM reward head's $2.78\times$ fidelity gap at $\dt > 1$ biases the \emph{data} on which any critic trains, so downstream fixes cannot address the source. MBPO-style rollout truncation \citep{janner2019mbpo} limits compounding error but DreamerV3's actor-critic trains entirely within imagination with no real-data anchor. MOReL \citep{kidambi2020morel} and COMBO \citep{yu2021combo} penalize model uncertainty, but CIVO is not a high-uncertainty regime---the RSSM is \emph{confidently wrong} at $\dt > 1$, producing low-variance biased predictions that uncertainty penalties would not flag.

